 "result": "In this repo (a Flask-style framework named `tessel`), `request`, `session` and `g` reach templates in two ways.\n\n**How they get there**\n- **Jinja globals:** `Tessel.create_jinja_environment` in `src/tessel/app.py:493-503` puts the `request`, `session` and `g` proxies (plus `config`, `link_for` and `get_flashed_messages`) into `jinja_env.globals`. This is what makes them visible in imported templates.\n- **Default context injector:** `_base_template_vars()` in `src/tessel/templating.py:21` swaps `g` and `request` for the concrete objects, which is faster. It leaves `session` as the proxy, so `session.accessed` still gets set.\n- **Registration:** `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:184` pre-registers `_base_template_vars` in `template_ctx_injectors[None]`.\n- **When it runs:** `_render()` (`templating.py:123`) calls `app.fill_template_scope(ctx, context)` (`app.py:588`). That runs every injector for `None` plus the current request's bundles, then re-applies the values you passed to `render_template` so they take precedence.\n\n**Adding your own variables**\n- Decorate a function that returns a dict with `@app.ctx_injector`. It is defined as `Scaffold.ctx_injector` in `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:549-564` and is wrapped by `@setupmethod`.\n- On a bundle, `@bundle.ctx_injector` only applies to templates rendered from that bundle's views.\n- `@bundle.app_ctx_injector` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:643-653`) registers it app-wide from a bundle.\n\n```python\n@app.ctx_injector\ndef inject_user():\n    return {\"user\": g.get(\"user\")}\n```\n\nFor a static value or a function rather than per-render data, `jinja_env.globals` also works. The registration helper is at `src/tessel/sansio/app.py:825`.",
